--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE NOTE (no scope narrowing — covenant #2)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The manifest record for this unit extracted 0 panels / 0 charts because the web page file
delegates its body to sub-components (HeroGauges + TabNav + OverviewTab/DrivingTab/ChargingTab/
BatteryTab, themselves composing OverviewVehicleComparison / DrivingPerformanceCards /
DrivingTemperatureStats / ChargingDetailSection). Rather than ship only the 9 formal items, the
FULL web composition is reproduced region-for-region: the 6 hero gauges, the 4-tab control, and
every <GlassPanel> inside each tab — 30+ panels, 20+ charts (bar / grouped-bar / composed-trend /
pie / radar / scatter / area / line), 3 leaderboards, and the quick-links grid — each in the same
data + grouping + order, each with its own loading / empty / success handling. Charts use the P3
native Swift Charts wrappers (TSBarChart / TSComposedChart / TSScatterChart / TSLineChart /
TSAreaChart / TSPieChart / TSRadarChart / TSChartContainer) — never a WKWebView. Dual-Y-axis
recharts ComposedCharts are rendered as a readable count+trend stacked pair (the wrappers are
single-axis), preserving both series instead of flattening the smaller one.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PATH NOTE (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The prompt's templated output path (apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Analytics/**) does not match the
repo's actual SwiftUI source tree. The shared iOS/macOS app target compiles apps/apple/Sources/**
(project.yml), and every already-DONE sibling P7 page lives under Sources/Features/<Domain>/. This
page therefore ships under apps/apple/Sources/Features/Analytics/** + Tests/Unit/Features/Analytics/,
exactly mirroring the DONE siblings (Statistics / FleetCompare / Mileage / LifetimeStats / TrueCost).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NAVIGATION NOTE (no predecessor bypass — covenant #7)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web route /analytics is the canonical pathSegment of the AppRoute.analytics case, and .analytics
is a primary tab — so the Fleet Analytics page is the route's rightful owner. AnalyticsRouteRegistration
registers .analytics and is composed into TeslaSyncApp.swift immediately AFTER StatisticsRouteRegistration
(which only aliases onto .analytics via the /statistics parser alias), so the primary "Analytics" tab and
the /analytics deep link now render the canonical Fleet Analytics page. No AppRoute case was added or
removed; AppRouteParser aliases (/statistics -> .analytics, /analytics -> .analytics) are untouched, so
Tests/Unit/App/RouteTests stays green. The StatisticsPage sources, models, and tests are untouched and
still compile + pass.

